  "query_preview": "..Moisture values rose dramatically overnight as a \nseries of weak s/wvs, located well to our north, induced a surge \nover the southern deserts. The 18Z sounding from KFGZ indicated \nrobust moisture and instability values, along with some shear. We \nexpect a very active day as a result. Back-building storms may \nprolong the activity well into the night, especially south and \neast of Flagstaff.\n\nIn the wake of the convection today and tonight, we expect a quiet \nstart for Saturday, due to debris cloud and cooler temperatures. \nHowever, convection south of our CWA SAturday may push into the \narea Saturday evening, mainly the southern and southeastern zones.\n\nThis pattern continues off and on for the reminder of the forecast \nperiod. Occasional surges of moisture and s/wvs to our north will \nbasically alternate active and suppressed days through next Friday.",
